  "title": "Kimbanguism",
  "summary": "Kimbanguism began in 1921 around Simon Kimbangu, who started a mission of healing on 6 April 1921; that date is now taken as the founding of the church, known as the Kimbanguist Church (Eglise kimbanguiste). His ministry lasted only five months, until 12 September 1921, and the church arose under Belgian colonial rule. His hometown, Nkamba, is the church’s holy city.",
